# Ported benchmark harness (from 79:~/EnvFactory/scripts/eval + the official
# harness repos). The scripts themselves ARE tracked -- otherwise they exist
# only on the eval box and losing the instance loses them. What stays out:
#   - every *.env, already covered by the repo-wide rule at the top of this
#     file. Those are the files that hold, or are meant to hold, live
#     third-party API keys (mcp_atlas/keys.env is the one with real ones).
#     Only their *.env.template siblings are tracked -- copy a template and
#     fill it in locally. Never put a key in a script or a README instead.
#   - RESULTS.md / VERIFICATION.md, via the repo-wide *.md rule. They are the
#     79 box own eval records, so they stay local by that policy.
#   - benchmark repos and run outputs, which live outside the tree entirely
#     (/root/autodl-tmp/dataset/agent, /root/autodl-tmp/eval_runs).
# If a key ever does land in a commit, rotate it -- scrubbing history is not
# enough once it has been pushed, and origin here is a public repo.

# Generated task bank: teacher output cached to avoid re-paying for identical
# tasks. Reproducible from the teacher, large, and churns constantly.
task_bank/
task_bank_schema_v1/
